+ *
+ * A raise that carries code 0xE06D7363 is an MSVC `throw`, and its record
+ * holds everything needed to name the type: parameter 1 is the exception
+ * object and parameter 2 the ThrowInfo. On x86 every pointer in that chain
+ * is an absolute guest address, so the TypeDescriptor -- and the decorated
+ * type name stored eight bytes into it -- can be read directly.
+ *
